# Line endings are part of this repo's contract, not a cosmetic detail.
#
# Every committed data artefact is hash-verified against data/MANIFEST.csv by
# tests/check_manifest.py, which CI runs on Linux. If git normalised CRLF->LF on
# commit, a Windows working copy and a Linux checkout would hold different bytes and
# every recorded sha256 would fail. The build scripts run on Windows and emit CRLF in
# places, so the fix is to pin LF everywhere — in the repo AND in the working copy on
# every platform — and to compute the manifest digests over those same LF bytes.
#
# eol=lf (not just text=auto) is the load-bearing part: it forces LF on checkout even
# where core.autocrlf=true.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary: never touch, never diff as text.
*.zip   binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.gpkg  binary
*.pbf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary

# Large generated artefacts that are text but not worth diffing in review.
*.jsonl  -diff
data/MANIFEST.json -diff

# Shell scripts and git hooks run in Linux CI and in containers: LF is mandatory.
*.sh        text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
